    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the prime factorisation of $280$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$280=2^3\\times5\\times7$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}280&=2\\times140\\\\280&=2\\times2\\times70\\\\280&=2\\times2\\times2\\times35\\\\280&=2^3\\times5\\times7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the least positive integer $n$ for which $280n$ is a perfect square.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n=70$.\n\nMultiply by $2\\times5\\times7$ to make every prime exponent even.",
          "worked": "Since $280=2^3\\times5\\times7$, an additional factor of each of $2$, $5$ and $7$ is required to make every prime exponent even. Thus the least value is\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=2\\times5\\times7\\\\n&=70.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck:\n$$\\begin{align*}280n&=2^4\\times5^2\\times7^2\\\\280n&=140^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the least positive integer $n$ for which $\\frac{280}{n}$ is a perfect square.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n=70$.\n\nThe largest square factor of $280$ is $4$, so $n=280\\div4$.",
          "worked": "Write $\\frac{280}{n}=k^2$, so $280=nk^2$. To minimise $n$, choose the largest square factor $k^2$ of $280=2^3\\times5\\times7$. The largest square factor is $2^2=4$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=\\frac{280}{4}\\\\n&=70.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{280}{70}&=4\\\\\\frac{280}{70}&=2^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
